                            CONTRIBUTING
Changes require an RFC (request for comments) before a PR. Post your proposal to
the engineering team at contact@podomy.com.

This includes new subsystems, protocol changes, and architectural
decisions. PRs opened without a prior group discussion will be redirected there
before code review.

Use GitHub Issues for bugs and actionable tasks. Tag issues with
good-first-issue if they are suitable for newcomers.

                         Review Expectations

Small PR (bugfix)       3 business days
Normal PR               7 days
RFC                     7 days

If maintainers cannot meet the window, they will say so. Silence is
not a no.

                          Getting Started
Prerequisites  Go >=1.26.3 (go.work:1) and golangci-lint v2
+               Install: https://golangci-lint.run/welcome/install/

1. Build        go build .
2. Verify       go run ./check/   # tidy + golangci-lint fmt (gofumpt/goimports @.golangci.yml:7) + goheader fix + golangci-lint run + go test + git diff --exit-code
               # or: golangci-lint fmt ./... && golangci-lint run ./...
3. Hook         git config core.hooksPath .githooks   # runs verify on git commit via .githooks/pre-commit:3
4. Test         go test ./...   # already in verify
5. Pick an issue or go over the code
6. Send an RFC to contact@podomy.com if the change is not small
7. Submit a PR
